# Quick Focaccia Bread

Status: Untested

## Recipe Name:
Quick Focaccia Bread (same day)

## Servings:
1 loaf, 16 servings, in a 9 x 13 inch pan

## Prep Time:
20 minutes

## Cook Time:
20 to 22 minutes, plus 3 hours rising

## Ingredients:
### Dough
- 420 g bread flour (3 cups)
- 1/2 tablespoon active dry yeast
- 1/2 tablespoon kosher salt
- 354 ml warm water (1 1/2 cups)
- 1 tablespoon olive oil
- Olive oil, for the pan

### Brine
- 1 tablespoon olive oil
- 1/2 tablespoon water
- 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt

### Topping
- 1 rosemary sprig, leaves chopped
- 1/2 shallot, minced

Use bread flour, not all-purpose. The higher protein is what gives focaccia its chew. Do not skip the generous oil in the pan: that oil fries the bottom crust, and the bottom crust is the point.

## Instructions:
1. Mix the dough. In a large bowl, stir together the bread flour, yeast, and kosher salt. Add the warm water and the olive oil. Stir with a wooden spoon or a dough whisk until a sticky dough forms.
2. Fold. With wet hands, lift the bottom of the dough and wrap it over the top a few times. Make a loose ball and work in any dry flour. Leave it in the bowl and cover with a clean dish towel.
3. First rise. Let it rise in a warm spot for 2 hours, until doubled and bubbly. It should jiggle when you shake the bowl.
4. Put it in the pan. Grease the bottom and sides of a metal 9 x 13 inch pan generously with olive oil. With oiled hands, turn the dough into the pan. Press and stretch it toward the edges. The corners can stay rounded. Keep the thickness even and do not knock the air out.
5. Second rise. Cover the pan with a dish towel, pulled tight so it does not touch the dough. Rest 1 hour in a warm spot.
6. Preheat. 30 minutes into the second rise, heat the oven to 425 F with a pizza stone on the centre rack.
7. Brine and top. After the hour, whisk the olive oil, water, and kosher salt in a small bowl. Pour the brine over the dough. Press your oiled fingers all the way down to the bottom of the pan to make deep dimples. Sprinkle the rosemary and shallot evenly over the top.
8. Bake. Set the pan on the hot pizza stone. Bake 20 to 22 minutes, until the top is deeply golden brown.
9. Cool. Let it cool completely in the pan or on a wire rack before you cut it.

Dimple all the way down. Shallow dimples even out in the oven and leave you with a flat top.

Source: Sonja Overhiser, "Quick Focaccia Bread (Same Day!)". A Couple Cooks. https://www.acouplecooks.com/quick-focaccia-bread/

